            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Locally Grown"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't add the cinnamon, because I tasted the beans prior to baking and thought they were perfect without it. This recipe, sans cinnamon, is my new favorite beans recipe! I usually find baked beans to be too sweet, but this recipe is easy on the sugar, and the chipotle peppers add a complex smoky kick to the mix. I can't wait to take these to my family reunion..."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ArtsySpoon2107"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is one of my all-time favorite dishes. I made it as written (minus the cinnamon) the first time. The second time I omitted the cinnamon again but added in 3 tofu hot dogs cut in approximately 1/2\" coins to the mix before baking. Loved it! I'm having it again tonight (again no cinnamon) only with 4 tofu hot dogs added in. Can't wait!!!",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-19T19:45:16.920Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kellieann"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I cut the amount of chipotle peppers in half and it was still too spicy for us.",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-13T18:11:16.203Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kikikins1234"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fabulous recipe! Huge hit with everyone alongside a smoked brisket. Did not use the cinnamon - sounded totally weird and then I read the reviews... my gut is usually right on... whenever I get a can of chipotles in adobo, I wiz it up in the processor and then freeze in ice cube trays. We like to use them in so much, but I refuse to waste the can...",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-18T11:29:08.263Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "1"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brandy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Sorry, but I didn't like this recipe at all. I just finished preparing this and I am afraid they would go to waste. I was hesitant about the cinnamon and I should have go with my gut feelings and omitted it. I like cinammon just not on beans. Ugh Yikes!! As this was cooking I knew I was going to hate it. It smell gross!!. To try to masquerade the cinammon taste I added onion powder, garlic, cilantro, liquid smoke, bell pepper and some ham flavored seasoning I had. Still the cinammon taste lingered a bit and it just taste terrible!!! Sorry :(. It sounded really good. Maybe next time, if I ever make this again, I will omit the cinammon",
            "datePublished": "2008-02-06T17:49:06.000Z"
          }
